% Homeowners underwriting guidelines of National General (Integon National
% Insurance Company) for California: the "Eligibility" pages (2-8) of the
% "California Premier and OneChoice Homeowners Underwriting & Product Guide",
% revised 14 January 2020. The guide is a grid of topics (the applicant,
% occupancy, protection class, roof, electrical, heating, plumbing, pets,
% pools, construction, coast, brush), each saying what is ineligible and what
% must be referred to underwriting. A guideline program of the homeowners
% model: it includes homeowners.le. A guideline is named after the guide's
% own heading ("roof", "brush rules").
%
% What is encoded (see DETAILS.md for the count):
% - read from the proposal's facts: every topic of pages 3-8 below;
% - the brush rules as a decision table (FireLine score and WillisRe score
%   give Accept, "Accept per UW review" or Decline); "Accept per UW review"
%   is read as a referral;
% - a finding someone records: a dog "showing aggressive tendencies";
% - not encoded: the property limits and coverage levels of page 2 (they
%   choose a product and a price, not whether a risk is written) other than
%   the two referrals on the dwelling limit and the personal property limit;
%   scheduled personal property, excess liability, watercraft and
%   recreational vehicles (other coverages); the brush factors the guide
%   lists after the table without saying how they count (elevation, brush
%   density, Santa Ana winds, debris).
% The guide leaves one cell of the brush table empty: a FireLine score of 3
% with a WillisRe score of exactly 1.00 is neither "< 1.00" nor "> 1.00".
% No row answers, and the model's own rule "brush score outside the table"
% refers such a proposal (scenario brush_gap in california_cases.le).
%
% The text is in sources/natgen_ca_homeowners.txt (the first ten pages of
% the PDF beside it). The guide was retrieved from an agency's website, not
% from SERFF: see DETAILS.md, "Sources".
%
% DISCLAIMER. This program is an example of Logical English. It is provided
% "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including any
% warranty that it is accurate, complete, up to date or fit for a particular
% purpose. It is not an official reading of the underwriting guidelines it
% cites, it is not an underwriting decision of any insurer, and it is not
% legal or insurance advice. Its answers may be wrong: do not rely on them
% for a real application; consult the insurer and a licensed agent. Its
% authors accept no liability for any loss or damage arising from its use.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base california includes these resources:
    homeowners.

the templates are:
    the applicant of *a proposal* has a history of *an offence*; undefined.
    the occupation of the applicant of *a proposal* is *an occupation*; undefined.
    the prior coverage of *a proposal* lapsed in the past year; undefined.
    *a dwelling* was previously insured; undefined.
    *a proposal* is in the name of a trust; undefined.
    the dwelling limit of *a proposal* is *an amount*; undefined.
    the personal property limit of *a proposal* is *an amount*; undefined.
    the protection class of *a dwelling* is *a number*; undefined.
    *a dwelling* is *a number* miles from a fire department; undefined.
    *a dwelling* is built on a slope of *a number* degrees; undefined.
    *a dwelling* was built in *a year*; undefined.
    *a dwelling* has an underground oil storage tank; undefined.
    the plumbing of *a dwelling* is *a number* years old; undefined.
    the plumbing of *a dwelling* has been completely updated; undefined.
    the breed of *an animal* is *a breed*; undefined.
    *an animal* has a bite history; undefined.
    the trampoline at *a dwelling* is surrounded by safety netting; undefined.
    the trampoline at *a dwelling* stands on flat ground; undefined.
    the swimming pool at *a dwelling* is fenced with a self-locking gate; undefined.
    the diving board at *a dwelling* is *a number* inches above the water; undefined.
    the number of farm animals at *a dwelling* is *a number*; undefined.
    *a dwelling* is *a number* feet from the coast; undefined.
    *a dwelling* is *a number* feet above the high water line; undefined.
    the fireline score of *a dwelling* is *a number*; undefined.
    the wildfire score of *a dwelling* is *a number*; undefined.
    the brush decision for fireline score *a number* with wildfire score *a second number* is *an action* under table brush.
    the brush decision for *a dwelling* is *an action*.
    *an animal* is of a listed breed.

the knowledge base california includes:

the National General California guide is published at "https://www.ironpointagent.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/uwg_ca_inic_ho-NatGen.pdf".
the text of the National General California guide is at "sources/natgen_ca_homeowners.txt".

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Property limits (page 2): only the two referrals.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule natgen_limit with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Refer any premier homes over $1,500,000":
a proposal must be referred to underwriting under property limits
    if the dwelling limit of the proposal is an amount
    and the amount > 1500000.

rule natgen_contents_refer with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Refer to underwriting if Coverage C > Coverage A (HO3 only)":
a proposal must be referred to underwriting under contents limit
    if the dwelling limit of the proposal is an amount
    and the personal property limit of the proposal is an other amount
    and the other amount > the amount.

rule natgen_contents_ineligible with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Ineligible if Coverage C >200":
a proposal is ineligible under contents limit
    if the dwelling limit of the proposal is an amount
    and the personal property limit of the proposal is an other amount
    and a limit is the amount * 2
    and the other amount > the limit.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Applicant information (page 3)
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule natgen_arson with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Arson or Fraud Ineligible.":
a proposal is ineligible under applicant history
    if the applicant of the proposal has a history of an offence
    and the offence is in [arson, fraud].

rule natgen_occupation with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Refer to underwriting if professional athlete, entertainer, journalist, politician, or other high profile profession.":
a proposal must be referred to underwriting under occupation
    if the occupation of the applicant of the proposal is an occupation
    and the occupation is in [professional athlete, entertainer, journalist, politician].

rule natgen_lapse with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Refer to underwriting if coverage lapsed in the past year.":
a proposal must be referred to underwriting under previous cancellations
    if the prior coverage of the proposal lapsed in the past year.

rule natgen_prior with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Ineligible if property was not previously insured. (Not applicable to HO4)":
a proposal is ineligible under prior insurance
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and it is not the case that
        the dwelling was previously insured
    and it is not the case that
        the policy form of the proposal is renters.

rule natgen_losses with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "More than 0 claims in last 5 years.":
a proposal is ineligible under loss history
    if the proposal is dated a date
    and the applicant of the proposal had a claim on a claim date
    and a limit is 60 months after the claim date
    and the date is before or equal to the limit.

rule natgen_trusts with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Trusts Refer to underwriting.":
a proposal must be referred to underwriting under trusts
    if the proposal is in the name of a trust.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Occupancy (page 3)
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule natgen_families with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Three and four family units are ineligible.":
a proposal is ineligible under number of families
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the number of families in the dwelling is a number
    and the number > 2.

rule natgen_vacant with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Vacant/Foreclosed/For Sale Not eligible.":
a proposal is ineligible under occupancy
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the occupancy of the dwelling is an occupancy
    and the occupancy is in [vacant, foreclosed, for sale].

rule natgen_rented_primary with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Ineligible if primary home is rented.":
a proposal is ineligible under rentals
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the occupancy of the dwelling is rented.

rule natgen_rentals with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "All home/condominium rentals must be referred to underwriting.":
a proposal must be referred to underwriting under rentals
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the occupancy of the dwelling is an occupancy
    and the occupancy is in [rented, seasonal rental].

rule natgen_day_care with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Home Day Care Ineligible.":
a proposal is ineligible under home day care
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the use of the dwelling is home day care.

rule natgen_timeshare with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Timeshares Ineligible.":
a proposal is ineligible under timeshares
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the use of the dwelling is timeshare.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Protection class and location (page 4, page 7)
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule natgen_pc9 with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Protection Class 9 is an underwriting referral.":
a proposal must be referred to underwriting under protection class
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the protection class of the dwelling is 9.

rule natgen_pc10 with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Ineligible risks in Protection Class 10.":
a proposal is ineligible under protection class
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the protection class of the dwelling is 10.

rule natgen_fire_department with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Properties be within 5 miles of fire department.":
a proposal is ineligible under protection class
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the dwelling is a number miles from a fire department
    and the number > 5.

rule natgen_slope with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Ineligible approval required if residence built on a slope of more than 30":
a proposal is ineligible under slope
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the dwelling is built on a slope of a number degrees
    and the number > 30.

rule natgen_coast with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Refer if less than 1,000 feet from the coast and less than 25 feet above high":
a proposal must be referred to underwriting under coastal guidelines
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the dwelling is a number feet from the coast
    and the number < 1000
    and the dwelling is an other number feet above the high water line
    and the other number < 25.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The dwelling (pages 4-6)
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule natgen_historic with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Homes listed on any historic registries are ineligible.":
a proposal is ineligible under historic home
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the dwelling is listed on a historic register.

rule natgen_age with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Home is ineligible if age of home is greater than 75 years.":
a proposal is ineligible under age of home
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the age of the dwelling is a number years
    and the number > 75.

rule natgen_construction with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "The following risks are ineligible: mobile homes, manufactured homes, underground or earth homes, fiberglass, yurts, balloon constructions":
a proposal is ineligible under types of construction
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the construction of the dwelling is a construction
    and the construction is in [mobile home, manufactured home, underground, earth home, fiberglass, yurt, balloon frame].

rule natgen_eifs with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "EIFS if built prior to 2000":
a proposal is ineligible under types of construction
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the construction of the dwelling is synthetic stucco
    and the dwelling was built in a year
    and the year < 2000.

rule natgen_log with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Log homes in Protection Class 9 are unacceptable.":
a proposal is ineligible under types of construction
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the construction of the dwelling is log
    and the protection class of the dwelling is 9.

rule natgen_foundation with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "The following types of foundations are ineligible: pilings, piers, wharves, jetties, on stilts or posts, or open foundations.":
a proposal is ineligible under types of foundation
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the foundation of the dwelling is a foundation
    and the foundation is in [pilings, piers, wharves, jetties, stilts, posts, open].

rule natgen_under_construction with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Ineligible for new business.":
a proposal is ineligible under dwelling under construction
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the dwelling is under construction.

rule natgen_renovation with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Homes undergoing renovation must be referred to underwriting.":
a proposal must be referred to underwriting under dwelling under construction
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the dwelling is undergoing renovation.

% The roof.
rule natgen_roof_material with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Wood, tar paper, rolled, plywood boards, stapled roofs, and asbestos":
a proposal is ineligible under roof
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the roof of the dwelling is made of a material
    and the material is in [wood shake, wood shingle, tar paper, rolled roofing, plywood boards, stapled roofing, asbestos].

rule natgen_roof_age with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Roof is older than 20 years, unless slate or tile":
a proposal is ineligible under roof
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the roof of the dwelling is a number years old
    and the number > 20
    and the roof of the dwelling is made of a material
    and it is not the case that
        the material is in [slate, tile].

rule natgen_roof_layers with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Refer to underwriting if roof has more than one layer of material.":
a proposal must be referred to underwriting under roof
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the roof of the dwelling has a number layers
    and the number > 1.

% Electrical.
rule natgen_amps with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Dwelling does not have minimum of 100 amps and 220 volt service":
a proposal is ineligible under electrical
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the electrical service of the dwelling is a number amps
    and the number < 100.

rule natgen_knob_and_tube with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Knob & tube or aluminum wiring present":
a proposal is ineligible under electrical
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the dwelling has knob and tube wiring.

rule natgen_aluminum with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Knob & tube or aluminum wiring present":
a proposal is ineligible under electrical
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the dwelling has aluminum wiring.

rule natgen_panel with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Presence of Federal Pacific Stab Lok or Zinsco electrical panels.":
a proposal is ineligible under electrical
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the electrical panel of the dwelling is a panel
    and the panel is in [Federal Pacific Stab Lok, Zinsco].

% Heating.
rule natgen_central_heat with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Must have central heat, properly installed":
a proposal is ineligible under heating
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the primary heat source of the dwelling is a source
    and it is not the case that
        the source is in [central heating, solar heating].

rule natgen_solar with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "All risks with Solar Heat sources must be referred":
a proposal must be referred to underwriting under heating
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the primary heat source of the dwelling is solar heating.

rule natgen_stoves with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Solid fuel burning stoves are ineligible":
a proposal is ineligible under heating
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the dwelling has a heater as a secondary heat source
    and the heater is in [woodstove, pellet stove, coal stove, kerosene stove].

rule natgen_oil_tank with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Underground oil storage tanks are ineligible.":
a proposal is ineligible under heating
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the dwelling has an underground oil storage tank.

% Plumbing.
rule natgen_plumbing_material with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Polybutylene, galvanized steel, or lead plumbing":
a proposal is ineligible under plumbing
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the plumbing of the dwelling is a material
    and the material is in [polybutylene, galvanized steel, lead].

rule natgen_plumbing_age with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Plumbing that is more than 40 years old and has not been completely updated.":
a proposal is ineligible under plumbing
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the plumbing of the dwelling is a number years old
    and the number > 40
    and it is not the case that
        the plumbing of the dwelling has been completely updated.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Additional exposures (pages 5-6)
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule natgen_breeds with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Dogs: Akita, American Bulldog, Chow, Doberman, Mastiff (All), Pit Bull (All), Presa Canario, Rottweiler, Wolf, or any mix of the above breeds":
a proposal is ineligible under pets
    if the household of the proposal keeps an animal
    and the animal is of a listed breed.

an animal is of a listed breed
    if the breed of the animal is a breed
    and the breed is in [Akita, American Bulldog, Chow, Doberman, Mastiff, Pit Bull, Presa Canario, Rottweiler, Wolf].

rule natgen_bites with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Dogs that have caused prior liability losses or that have bite history":
a proposal is ineligible under pets
    if the household of the proposal keeps an animal
    and the animal has a bite history.

rule natgen_aggressive with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Dogs showing aggressive tendencies.":
a proposal is ineligible under pets
    if the household of the proposal keeps an animal
    and the species of the animal is dog
    and it is not the case that
        the animal is of a listed breed
    and the finding aggressive tendencies about the animal is established.

rule natgen_wild with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Any wild animals.":
a proposal is ineligible under pets
    if the household of the proposal keeps an animal
    and the species of the animal is a species
    and it is not the case that
        the species is in [dog, cat, horse, bird, fish, rabbit].

rule natgen_trampoline with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Trampolines are acceptable subject to the following conditions:":
a proposal is ineligible under trampolines
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the premises of the dwelling include trampoline
    and it is not the case that
        the trampoline at the dwelling is surrounded by safety netting
            and the trampoline at the dwelling stands on flat ground.

rule natgen_pool_fence with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Pool is fenced in with a self-locking gate":
a proposal is ineligible under swimming pools
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the premises of the dwelling include swimming pool
    and it is not the case that
        the swimming pool at the dwelling is fenced with a self-locking gate.

rule natgen_diving_board with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "There are no diving boards greater than 18 inches above the water":
a proposal is ineligible under swimming pools
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the diving board at the dwelling is a number inches above the water
    and the number > 18.

rule natgen_ramps with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Presence of skateboard or bicycle ramps on premises":
a proposal is ineligible under attractive nuisances
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the premises of the dwelling include a hazard
    and the hazard is in [skateboard ramp, bicycle ramp].

rule natgen_treehouse with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Refer to underwriting when home has a treehouse on the premises.":
a proposal must be referred to underwriting under attractive nuisances
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the premises of the dwelling include treehouse.

rule natgen_farming with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Refer to underwriting if more than 2 farm animals.":
a proposal must be referred to underwriting under farming
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the number of farm animals at the dwelling is a number
    and the number > 2.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Brush rules (page 8): a decision table.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

the table brush is, with first match, with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "A risk may be classified as being ineligible due to Wildfire exposure area":
    row | fireline | wildfire                | action   | confer
    b01 | 0        | < 2.5                   | accept   | "0 <2.50 Accept"
    b02 | 0        | >= 2.5 and <= 4         | refer    | "0 2.50 to 4.00 Accept per UW review"
    b03 | 0        | > 4                     | decline  | "0 > 4.00 Decline"
    b11 | 1        | < 1                     | accept   | "1 < 1.00 Accept"
    b12 | 1        | >= 1 and <= 2           | refer    | "1 1.00 to 2.00 Accept per UW review"
    b13 | 1        | > 2                     | decline  | "1 > 2.00 Decline"
    b21 | 2        | < 0.75                  | accept   | "2 < .75 Accept"
    b22 | 2        | >= 0.75 and <= 1.5      | refer    | "2 .75 to 1.50 Accept per UW review"
    b23 | 2        | > 1.5                   | decline  | "2 > 1.50 Decline"
    b31 | 3        | < 1                     | refer    | "3 < 1.00 Accept per UW review"
    b32 | 3        | > 1                     | decline  | "3 > 1.00 Decline"
    b40 | >= 4     | any                     | decline  | "Note: FireLine Scores 4 and above are always unacceptable."

the brush decision for a dwelling is an action
    if the fireline score of the dwelling is a number
    and the wildfire score of the dwelling is a second number
    and the brush decision for fireline score the number with wildfire score the second number is the action under table brush.

rule natgen_brush_decline with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Brush Rules":
a proposal is ineligible under brush rules
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the brush decision for the dwelling is decline.

rule natgen_brush_review with provenance the National General California guide,
        confer "Accept per UW review":
a proposal must be referred to underwriting under brush rules
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the brush decision for the dwelling is refer.

% The model's own rule, not the guide's: scores the table has no row for go
% to an underwriter.
a proposal must be referred to underwriting under brush score outside the table
    if the proposal is for a dwelling
    and the fireline score of the dwelling is a number
    and the wildfire score of the dwelling is a second number
    and it is not the case that
        the brush decision for the dwelling is an action.
